  "historical_output_text": " I was a junior in high school and had always been quite meticulous about my appearance. I had been raised in a family where neatness and order were highly valued, and I took pride in my ability to maintain a polished look. It was a minor mistake, really - a small stain on my shirt that I had somehow missed during my daily routine. \n\nI didn't notice it at first, as I was rushing to catch the bus. The morning sun was blinding and I was preoccupied with getting to school on time. But when I arrived and looked in the mirror at my locker, there it was - a small dark splotch on my otherwise spotless white shirt. I panicked for a moment. \n\nThat morning, I sat in class with my head down, feeling embarrassed. I could feel the eyes of my classmates on me as we waited for the teacher to arrive. I barely heard a word she said. I was too busy convincing myself that no one had noticed, that I could fix it later.\n\nAfter school, I spent the entire ride home staring out the window, wondering how to explain it to my mother. I debated whether to throw the shirt",
